From: Luckfox ALPR build <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] host: import the VFS symbol namespace (Rockchip/Android-derived kernels)

Rockchip's RV1106 kernel (Luckfox Pico SDK, Linux 5.10, Android-common based)
exports filp_open() and kernel_read() only in the symbol namespace
VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver. The host driver uses
them for host-side ESP firmware OTA (main.c), so modpost fails with:

  ERROR: modpost: module esp32_sdio uses symbol kernel_read from namespace
  VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver, but does not import it.

Importing a namespace that a kernel doesn't define is harmless, so this is safe
on other kernels too. (Linux >= 6.13 spells it MODULE_IMPORT_NS("..."); this
patch targets the 5.10 Luckfox kernel.)

---
 host/main.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/host/main.c b/host/main.c
--- a/host/main.c
+++ b/host/main.c
@@ -2280,5 +2280,10 @@ MODULE_AUTHOR("Yogesh Mantri <yogesh.mantri@espressif.com>");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Kapil Gupta <kapil.gupta@espressif.com>");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Wifi driver for ESP-Hosted solution");
 MODULE_VERSION(RELEASE_VERSION);
+#ifdef MODULE_IMPORT_NS
+/* filp_open()/kernel_read() (host-side OTA) live in this namespace on
+ * Android-derived kernels such as Rockchip's RV1106 5.10. */
+MODULE_IMPORT_NS(VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver);
+#endif
 module_init(esp_init);
 module_exit(esp_exit);
